From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:01:07 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: report short GI for HT and VHT ratespecs

Preserve the firmware short-GI bit when converting HT and VHT ratespecs
to cfg80211 rate information. Without it, nl80211 reports the long-GI
bitrate even when the ratespec requests short GI; VHT MCS9 NSS2 at
40 MHz is reported as 360 instead of 400 Mbit/s.

Only interpret this bit for HT and VHT. The same bit has different
meanings for other encodings, whose guard intervals retain their
existing handling.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 4cf1b7cb0c983e3b81934ffb4ff0dfd6978d98b1)
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
index 4b5c6d870e..f5cd39ea63 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -3210,6 +3210,10 @@ static void brcmf_convert_ratespec_to_rateinfo(u32 ratespec,
 		/* Fill in nothing */
 		break;
 	}
+	if ((BRCMF_RSPEC_ISHT(ratespec) || BRCMF_RSPEC_ISVHT(ratespec)) &&
+	    BRCMF_RSPEC_ISSGI(ratespec))
+		rateinfo->flags |= RATE_INFO_FLAGS_SHORT_GI;
+
 	if (BRCMF_RSPEC_ISHT(ratespec)) {
 		rateinfo->flags |= RATE_INFO_FLAGS_MCS;
 		rateinfo->mcs = ratespec & BRCMF_RSPEC_HT_MCS_MASK;
